            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0566" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15 Arms Truce/27: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-21T20:00:00+01:00">September 21, 1931—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 21—6:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>150. At this afternoon’s meeting of the Third Committee, after welcoming the
                    representative of the United States, the Chairman recommended that the debate on
                    the truce proposal be confined to an explanation by Colonel Inhaling [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Colban?</hi>] of Norway of intended purpose of the
                    Scandinavian resolution, and to a declaration by General de <pb facs="0567"
                        n="453" xml:id="pg453"/> Marinis<anchor n="62" xml:id="d338-f1"/> [omission]
                    spoke in the sense of my 132, September 26 [<hi rendition="#italic">16</hi>], 5
                    p.m., stating that he would submit an amendment to the Scandinavian resolution
                    which will be shortly circulated. Discussion on this question will be resumed
                    tomorrow afternoon. Inasmuch as Marinis’ proposals were not generally known few
                    of the delegates have definite views as yet as to what attitude they will
                    adopt.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d338-f1" n="62" xml:id="d338-f1-content">
                <p>General Alberto de Marinis, member of the Italian Senate; Italian representative
                    on the Third Committee.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
